steps.description:
src/cli/commands/status.ts:18-21 emits the invalid-status error without the `plot status: ` prefix that every other command uses for its error messages (see attach.ts:21, answer.ts:23, append.ts:59, etc.).

Current line:
  io.err(`invalid status ${JSON.stringify(next)} (expected one of ${PLOT_STATUSES.join(", ")})\n`);

Fix: change to
  io.err(`plot status: invalid status ${JSON.stringify(next)} (expected one of ${PLOT_STATUSES.join(", ")})\n`);

Update any matching assertion in src/cli/router.test.ts (search for `invalid status`). No other call sites depend on the exact wording.
